      {
        "slide": 1,
        "role": "cover",
        "subject": "A deep violet powder-coated server rack standing on a magenta-to-violet studio sweep. Its hex-perforated door is swung open to the right with a clipped paper page on it, and the page has one orange highlighted line. Inside are a patch panel of colored cables spilling down the right rail, rows of drive sleds with cyan LEDs and handles, and a blue status panel at the base. A short stack of three kraft-wrapped reams under a pale sheet block sits at the rack's left foot.",
        "visual_consequence": "Without the headline, the reader sees the machine the rule is about with its door open and a paper page pinned to it, and a small pile of the same wrapped paper that grows across the deck. That links the server to a document and an estimate. The new dek reads cleanly at 100 percent in six lines of light sans on the violet field, with no clipping, overlap or stray punctuation.",
        "weakness": "Secondary only. The rack reads as finished hardware. Remaining defects: the interior shading is almost one violet hue, the clipped register page is a flat bright card with no curl or thickness, the top sheet block is a featureless pale slab, a thin hot-pink glow line runs along the bottom of the open door, and an empty violet band sits between the headline and the dek.",
        "repair": "None required for acceptance. If polished later, give the top sheet block visible sheet-edge lines and the clipped page a slight curl and edge thickness.",
